WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668 size:78% position:39%
-Many of us this year
have had to adjust

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
to new working conditions,
which in a lot of cases

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.940
includes working remotely,
and while I can appreciate

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're still learning
to navigate this,

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
recently, one of my writers,
Mike Scollins,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
committed the cardinal sin
of working from home --

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
he wore a tank top
to a Zoom meeting.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here to talk about it is
that writer -- Mike Scollins

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.424 size:75% position:38%
Mike, how you doing?
-I've been better.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it because we made fun
of you relentlessly

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.862 line:92%
for wearing a tank top on Zoom

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What happened to me was not
making fun.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was an assault.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.101 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Was it really that bad?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't know.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's see an artist's renderin
of the day in question.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't remember my arms being
quite that scrawny.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks a lot,
graphics department.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I wouldn't say
it's inaccurate.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.047 line:92%
-Okay, just take it down.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.650
I'd like to run through a list
of my so-called friends on staff

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.486 line:92%
and see what they have to say.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.889 line:92%
This is head writer Alex Baze.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I explained I was
wearing a tank top

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.392
'cause I thought I was
in the Zoom waiting room,

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
he said, "Do you mean the Zoom
weight room?"

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.330 line:92%
-Oh, that's a great burn.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.900
-They're all great burns.
The quality of the burns

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.868 line:92%
is not what this is about.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is Karen Chee.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.872
She's 4'11", but turns out
she can still dunk on me.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I defended the tank
and said I thought it was nice

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
she said,
"If you like it so much,

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.846 line:92%
why'd you cut the sleeves off?

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Good one, Chee.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, guess what, Karen?
You went to Harvard,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.654
and I went to Manhattan College,
and we have the same job.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.422 line:92%
Now who makes bad decisions?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.523 line:92%
-I mean, she got the job,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, right out of
college though.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bryan Donaldson,
shown here in a screen gra

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.765
from "To Catch a Predator" said,
"If you like it so much,

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
why didn't you buy
the rest of it?"

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.302 size:88% position:44%
It's the only question
he's ever asked besides,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Have you tried resetting
the router?"

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Mike Shoemaker.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, come on, that is not
Mike Shoemaker.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Similar vibe though.
Similar vibe.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ally Hord.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
She texted, "Getting attacke
is the pits,"

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
a clear reference
to my visible armpit hair.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.555 line:92%
-Ally Hord from the top rope

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.457
-Be glad it was over Zoom, Ally,
'cause I use

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:08.561
Tom's of Maine deodorant, an
the way it works is, it doesn't.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.697
Also, if you're wondering wh
she's smiling in that photo,

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was taken the minute sh
found out Tom Hanks had COVID.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That is not true.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.203 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Sounds true though.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.405 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Next! Amber Ruffin!

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
She decided to take my tank to
burns national.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:23.877 line:92%
Let's see what she had to say.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not going to name names
but obviously someone --

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.747 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mike Scollins!

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Showed up on Zoom
in a tank top.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.721
-You were supposed to be
promoting your show, Amber

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not why you were
invited on.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's partially why she wa
invited on.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.295 line:92%
-That brings me to you, Seth

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.330 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Roll the clip, Wally.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.432 line:92%
-Scollins, I do cue cards.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You, too?
Seriously?

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Somebody roll it.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.204 line:92%
-I mean, look at your outfit

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look like Mike Scollin
in a Zoom meeting.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.976 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Unbelievable!

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not even the type
of tank I like.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those sleeves are clearly cut.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:04.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, Seth, you know what els
could use some clear cuts?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"A Closer Look."

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You about finished, pal?
-Nope.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seth, do you know why I wear
a tank top on Zoom?

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know. 'Cause you don'
think things through?

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:17.664
-I wear a tank top on Zoom for
the little kid watching at hom

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
who clearly does not
have the arms

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:22.235
to pull something like that off,
but he does it anyway.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sorry. How is a kid watchin
our Zoom meeting?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:28.608
-I do it for the little kid in
the Midwest who, all his life,

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been told he needs to hide
his weird chest hair.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.646 line:92%
-What little kid has chest hair?

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know.
He's like Italian.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Scollins.
-Seth, tank tops

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
aren't just for lifeguards
or stepdads

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:42.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
or guys who want you to know
"If you can read this,

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.791 size:81% position:41% line:92%
my old lady fell off."

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're for Scollins'
and Karnells' --

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another writer who wears
tank tops but gets a free pass

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.865
-And, of course, the folks
who just don't feel like

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.768
getting dressed for a Zoom
meeting, God bless them.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:59.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, Mike, I hate
to cut you off --

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was that a --
-It was.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:04.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right. We're done here.
We're done.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey, Mike?

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.248 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah?

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Tanks!

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I hate you.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mike Scollins,
ladies and gentlemen!

